            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am afraid, this is impossible to fix and is just how extmarks work in Neovim. Th diagnostics shows separate virtual line which fully \"owns\" what is displayed on that line. I am pretty sure there is currently not way to workaround that and no plans to allow this kind of functionality in core.\n\nClosing as upstream Neovim's issue.",
